# Local IDE and System Settings
.vscode/
.kiro/
.serena/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Agent tooling. Personal, machine-specific, and this repository goes public at
# v1.0.0 — `.mcp.json` records absolute local paths.
#
# `.claude/` is deny-by-default because the tooling keeps adding machine-specific
# files there without asking: `settings.local.json` (per-machine permission
# overrides), `scheduled_tasks.lock` and `worktrees/` are the ones seen so far, and
# an exception list silently exposes whatever it has not heard of yet. Only a
# shared, reviewable project config is re-included.
#
# It must be `.claude/*`, not `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the directory form makes the negation below do nothing.
.mcp.json
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json

# Playwright MCP drops page snapshots here, in whatever directory the session
# was started from. Transient agent scratch output, never project artifacts.
.playwright-mcp/

# Build and Compilation Outputs
dist/
build/
out/

# Packed tarballs. `scripts/check-pack.mjs` already packs into an OS-temp scratch
# directory, so this covers a *manual* `npm pack`, which writes to the current
# directory by default. Prefer `--pack-destination` outside the repo anyway: `main`
# gets force-push protection because the commit history is the clean-room evidence
# of independent derivation, so a binary committed by accident is effectively
# permanent. `*.gz` is deliberately NOT ignored — CLAUDE.md requires the arXiv
# LaTeX source to live outside this repository, and hiding a stray copy would turn
# a visible licence problem into an invisible one.
*.tgz

# Dependency Directories
node_modules/
jspm_packages/
web_modules/

# Logs and Diagnostics
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# Environment and Secrets (Never commit these!)
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local

# TypeScript / Testing caching
.eslintcache
.tsbuildinfo
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage/

# Subagent-driven-development scratch workspace (ledgers, briefs, review packages)
.superpowers/

# Raw benchmark output. The harness and the figures worth keeping are recorded by hand in
# bench/RESULTS.md, which is committed - a number without its harness is unusable.
bench/*.json
